    "description": "Title:\nAssorted Teal Glass Insulators Colorado Springs Cripple Creek Toll Line\nDepartment:\nAdults\nCondition:\nUsed\nCondition Description:\nUsed - shows some wear and patina\nStyle:\nVintage\nColor:\nTeal\nCategory:\nCollectibles & Art\nType:\nGlass Insulator\nDesign:\nTextured glass\nFeatures:\nAssorted shapes and shades\nMaterial:\nGlass\nSet Includes:\nGlass insulators, wooden base\nShape:\nAssorted\nTheme:\nVintage Electrical\nDescription:\nAdd a unique piece of history to your space with this assortment of vintage teal glass insulators, once used to support overhead power lines. Each insulator in this set showcases distinct shapes, textures, and slightly different shades of teal and green, creating a captivating collection for display. Visible wear and patina reflect their authentic utility and age, enhancing their nostalgic character and appeal. One notable feature is a wooden base with a descriptive label, indicating these insulators were part of the Colorado Springs - Cripple Creek Toll Line, dated from 1910 to 1978. This historical detail adds an extra layer of interest, making the set especially attractive for collectors and history enthusiasts. Ideal for use as decorative accents on shelves, mantels, or desks, these insulators offer a charming way to incorporate industrial heritage into your home or office decor. This item is in used vintage condition and displays signs of wear consistent with age and previous use",
